// The Arch logo in Arch's own blue, and nothing else changed.
//
// fastfetch draws the logo out of the sixteen-colour palette by default, so on
// this system the arch mark came out in the spaceduck purple sitting in that
// slot. The obvious fix is the wrong one: moving a colour in the palette to
// suit one logo would change every program that asks for that slot, including
// the text console, whose table has to stay in step with kitty's for the
// tuigreet preview to mean anything.
//
// This changes nothing shared. `38;2;R;G;B` is a 24-bit SGR sequence, which
// kitty renders exactly as given without consulting the palette at all, so the
// mark is the only thing on screen that moves. 23,147,209 is #1793D1, the blue
// Arch uses for its own logo.
//
// The arch logo has one colour slot. If a logo with more than one is ever
// selected, the others stay at their defaults rather than being guessed at.
{
    "logo": {
        "color": {
            "1": "38;2;23;147;209"
        }
    }
}
